## Analysis Instructions

You are evaluating candidate CVs for the role described in the system context.
Read the entire CV carefully before scoring.

### Field Semantics

- `name`: Candidate's full name as written on the CV. Never infer or guess.
- `email`: Email address verbatim from the CV. Set to null if absent — do NOT guess.
- `undergrad_university`: Name of undergraduate institution. null if not on CV.
- `masters_university`: Name of Master's/PhD institution. null if none listed.
- `field_of_study`: Primary field (e.g. "Computer Science", "Electrical Engineering"). null if ambiguous.
- `still_in_school`: true if the CV shows an ongoing degree (no graduation date, or graduation date in the future).
- `years_experience`: Estimate total professional experience in years (float). null if completely unclear.
- `summary`: 2-3 sentence factual summary of the candidate's background and strongest signals.
- `score_rationale`: One sentence explaining the score BEFORE you assign it. Reference specific evidence from the CV.
- `fit_score`: Integer 1-10 based on the rubric below. Assigned AFTER writing score_rationale.

### Scoring Rubric

| Score | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| 9-10  | Exceptional match. Hits every must-have; strong nice-to-haves; top-tier background. |
| 7-8   | Strong candidate. Meets all must-haves; some nice-to-haves; recommend interview. |
| 5-6   | Partial fit. Meets most must-haves but notable gaps; possible stretch hire. |
| 3-4   | Weak fit. Missing key requirements; significant upskilling needed. |
| 1-2   | Poor fit. Fundamental mismatch in experience, domain, or seniority. |

Score candidates relative to the rubric bands, not relative to each other.
Do not cluster scores — use the full 1-10 range.

### Null Handling

Set any field to null if the information is not clearly stated on the CV.
Never infer, extrapolate, or hallucinate emails, institution names, or dates.

---

## Few-Shot Example

### Input CV (paraphrased)
> Alex Chen — alex.chen@email.com
> B.Sc. Computer Science, State University (2018)
> M.Sc. Machine Learning, Tech Institute (2020)
> 3.5 years as ML Engineer at MidCorp (2020–2023); led recommendation system rewrite.
> Currently: Senior ML Engineer at BigCo (2023–present).

### Expected Output
```json
{
  "name": "Alex Chen",
  "email": "alex.chen@email.com",
  "undergrad_university": "State University",
  "masters_university": "Tech Institute",
  "field_of_study": "Machine Learning",
  "still_in_school": false,
  "years_experience": 5.5,
  "summary": "ML engineer with a Master's in ML and 5+ years of industry experience. Led a recommendation system rewrite at MidCorp and currently a Senior ML Engineer at BigCo. Strong match for the ML domain.",
  "score_rationale": "Meets all must-haves (ML expertise, industry experience, Master's degree) with a concrete ownership example; no portfolio URL or open-source contributions visible on CV.",
  "fit_score": 8
}
```
